<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taurus Mountains</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Taurus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Taurus Mountains are a mountain range in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, separating the Anatolian plateau from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. They formed a natural barrier and frontier in many periods of history. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-apamea">Treaty of Apamea</a> of 188 BCE stripped the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucids</a> of their Anatolian lands beyond the Taurus and forbade them from waging war west of it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taurus-mountains.jpg" alt="Taurus Mountains" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zeynel Cebeci · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Demirkazik_Crest_of_Aladag_Mountains_in_Nigde_Turkey.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
